From: NanoKVM build <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] licheerv-nano: stage the boot FIT clear of the kernel run region

The NanoKVM image boots a single FIT (boot_<slot>.itb: kernel + FDT +
initramfs) rather than four separate files, so kernel_addr_r stops being a
place the kernel lands and becomes the place the whole FIT is staged before
bootm extracts from it. At the stock 0x81000000 the kernel's own run region
(0x80200000 upwards) grows into the staged image and bootm aborts with "new
format image overwritten - must RESET the board to recover".

Move it to 0x83000000, above the run region and below ramdisk_addr_r. That
leaves a 16 MiB staging window, which nanokvm-boot-fit asserts the FIT fits
into, and it decouples the two budgets: the kernel is bounded by
fdt_addr_r=0x82000000 rather than by wherever the FIT happens to be staged.

Also pin two environment defaults that the boot flow depends on:

  verify=yes, so FIT hash checking does not rest on env_get_yesno()
  returning -1 for an unset variable and -1 happening to be truthy.

  bootmeths=rauc, so the bootstd scan only ever offers the RAUC bootmeth.
  bootmeth_extlinux, _efiloader and _script stay compiled in -- they are
  worth having at the prompt when rescuing a board by hand -- but left in
  the scan order bootmeth_script would find the very same boot.scr on p1
  and source it with none of the slot variables set. Setting this in the
  compiled defaults rather than only in the stored environment means even
  a card with a blank or corrupt env scans in the right order.

Slot selection itself is not here. It was, briefly -- a hand-written nkvm_*
env script implementing try/swap/bootcount. Upstream's bootmeth_rauc owns
that now (BOOT_ORDER + BOOT_<slot>_LEFT, enabled from the u-boot recipe), so
the board header carries only the address plan.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [NanoKVM boot-flow specific]
---
--- a/include/configs/licheerv_nano.h
+++ b/include/configs/licheerv_nano.h
@@ -14,13 +14,41 @@
 
 #define CFG_SYS_SDRAM_BASE         0x80000000
 
+/*
+ * kernel_addr_r is the *staging* address for the whole boot FIT
+ * (boot_<slot>.itb: kernel + FDT + initramfs), not the kernel's run address.
+ * bootm extracts the kernel sub-image down to 0x80200000, so staging has to
+ * sit clear of the region the kernel is about to occupy. At the stock
+ * 0x81000000 it does not, and bootm aborts with "new format image overwritten
+ * - must RESET the board to recover".
+ *
+ * 0x83000000 puts the staged image above the run region and below
+ * ramdisk_addr_r, leaving a 16 MiB staging window that nanokvm-boot-fit
+ * asserts the FIT fits into. It also decouples the two: the kernel is now
+ * bounded by fdt_addr_r=0x82000000 rather than by where the FIT is staged.
+ *
+ * verify=yes pins FIT hash checking on. bootm already verifies by default,
+ * but only because env_get_yesno() returns -1 for an unset variable and -1 is
+ * truthy -- too incidental a mechanism to leave the integrity of the boot
+ * payload resting on.
+ *
+ * bootmeths=rauc holds the bootstd scan to the RAUC bootmeth. The others stay
+ * compiled in for hand rescue at the prompt, but in the scan order
+ * bootmeth_script would find the same boot.scr on p1 and source it without
+ * any of the slot variables set.
+ *
+ * Everything stays below bootm_size=0x9500000, i.e. under the ION carveout at
+ * 0x89500000 (see the ramdisk-addr patch).
+ */
 #define CFG_EXTRA_ENV_SETTINGS  "consoledev=ttyS0\0" \
 								"baudrate=115200\0" \
 								"bootm_size=0x9500000\0" \
 								"fdt_addr_r=0x82000000\0" \
-								"kernel_addr_r=0x81000000\0" \
+								"kernel_addr_r=0x83000000\0" \
 								"ramdisk_addr_r=0x84000000\0" \
 								"scriptaddr=0x80c00000\0" \
+								"verify=yes\0" \
+								"bootmeths=rauc\0" \
 								BOOTENV
 
 #endif /* __CONFIG_H */
